message.content:
**Rotating Card – CSS Only**

Below is a minimal example that shows how to create a card that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an HTML file or embed it in your project.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;          /* card width */
  height: 200px;         /* card height */
  perspective: 1000px;   /* gives depth to the 3D transform */
  margin: 50px auto;     /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- Card (the element that rotates) ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform .6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;    /* keep children in 3D space */
  position: relative;
}

/* ---------- Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card::before,
.card::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;                 /* top/right/bottom/left: 0 */
  backface-visibility: hidden; /* hide backside when rotated */
  border-radius: inherit;
}

.card::before {              /* front face */
  background: linear-gradient(135deg,#ff9a9e 0%,#fad0c4 100%);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
  font-weight: bold;
}

.card::after {               /* back face */
  background: linear-gradient(135deg,#a18cd1 0%,#fbc2eb 100%);
  transform: rotateY(180deg); /* place it behind the front */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
  font-weight: bold;
}

/* ---------- Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg); /* flip the card */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card"></div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a *perspective* so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | The element that actually rotates. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3D space. |
| `::before` / `::after` | Two pseudo‑elements act as the front and back faces of the card. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis. |

Feel free to replace the gradients, text, or add more content inside the pseudo‑elements. If you need a different axis (X or Z), just change `rotateY` to `rotateX` or `rotateZ`. Enjoy!
